{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Waze 'Record your own voice' custom voice-pack script. Sourced verbatim from the Waze iOS app's Nepali-voice recording screen (screenshots, 2026-08-15): categories 'Start of drive', 'Distances', 'Instructions', 'Reports', 'Other', 43 English prompts, each with a natural-spoken-Nepali counterpart. Every phrase is a standalone clip (Waze's own '6 seconds max' constraint) meant to be concatenated at runtime with other clips (e.g. a distance clip followed by an instruction clip) - so wording must stay exactly this atomic, not merged into combined sentences like the main benchmark corpus.",
  "metadata_notes": {
    "waze_group": "The original Waze UI section this phrase was recorded under (Start of drive / Distances / Instructions / Reports / Other) - kept for traceability since it doesn't map 1:1 onto this project's 'category' field.",
    "tts_text": "Latin-script rendering of the Nepali portion, for engines/humans that cannot read Devanagari.",
    "review_status": "All Nepali entries are 'needs-review' - fresh translations authored for this task, following the naturalness principles in docs/nepali-human-review-v2.md, but not yet confirmed by a native speaker.",
    "content_principles": "Same as the main corpus: natural spoken Nepali, not literal translation. Notable choices: माइल (mile) kept as a loanword since Waze can run in imperial-unit locales; डेढ used for '1.5' instead of a decimal calque; रातो बत्तीमा क्यामेरा / बाटोबाट निस्कनुहोस् reuse the fixes proposed in nepali-human-review-v2.md rather than repeating the calques (निकास, रातो बत्ती क्यामेरा) originally in phrases.json."
  },
